! mcp_bootstrap_p108.strap -- MCP, printed page 108:
! "*** MISCELLANEOUS SYSTEM SYMBOLS ***".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.115, header READ not assumed: the
! top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP  CARD ID
! CD000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 108".
!
! TWELVE LINES, AND THE COUNT WAS CONFIRMED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints the card serial: line 1 is CD000001 and
! line 12 is CD000012, consecutive with no break.  MEASURED OVER THE
! WHOLE PAGE HEIGHT, not over the band the body was read from: the
! serial column (x 4600-4860 at 300 dpi) was rendered y=0..3300 and
! its ink profile has exactly THIRTEEN text runs -- twelve at the
! listing's 50-px line pitch (y 349..929) and one at y 3192, which
! is the form's own mirrored "IBM." imprint showing through from the
! back and not a row.  So nothing fell off the top or the bottom.
! (This mattered: the body render was -x 900 -W 4300 at 400 dpi,
! which stops at x 3900 in 300-dpi coords and does NOT include the
! serial column at all.  "The rest of the page looked blank" would
! not have been evidence -- see printed p.84's phantom 51-word gap.)
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE: "CD". <<<  printed p.103 was
! punching CA0000NN.  The card-serial prefix on this page is CD and
! the serial restarts at 000001, so this is the fourth deck of the
! assembly, not a continuation of p.103's.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS, AND WHY IT COMPILES NOT ONE BIT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-4 are comment cards: the asterisk box around the heading.
! Lines 5-12 are EIGHT SYN cards.  A SYN deposits no storage word, so
! this deck's entire check surface is EIGHT SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING
! ROWS -- the convention printed pp.24, 98, 99, 101 and 102
! established.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints "+00000000" and a
! data description ("NULL", "BU,30 ,10", "BU,01 ,10", "BU,07 ,10")
! on all eight rows; that is the column working correctly on a
! definitions page and it must NOT be faked into a !CHECK.
!
! >>> THE PROOF THAT THE LOCATION COLUMN IS PRINTING SYN VALUES AND
! NOT ADDRESSES DOES NOT REST ON THE TRAILING "+". <<<  It rests on
! the sequence, which a location counter cannot produce:
!
!     line  5   000040.00+
!     line  6   000000.00+      <-- BACKWARDS
!     line  7   000002.00+
!     line  8   000000.00+      <-- backwards again
!     line  9   000003.00+
!     line 10   000000.00+      <-- and a third time
!     line 11   000000.33+
!     line 12   000000.32+      <-- backwards by 1 bit
!
! A counter does not go down, and three different symbols do not
! share one address.  Every one of the eight is a RESOLVED SYN VALUE.
! The trailing "+" is the sign, printed as a suffix the way printed
! p.84's negative SYN prints "000001.00-"; it is dropped in the !SYM
! lines below because listing_oracle's loc_bits parses "word.bit" and
! has no sign field, which is what pp.99-102's decks do.
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS NOT PRINTED ON THIS PAGE, AND I AM NOT GUESSING
! WHERE THE COUNTER STANDS. <<<  There is no SLC row here.  The SLC
! written below is INERT SCAFFOLDING so the deck assembles
! standalone: nothing on this page consumes storage, and not one of
! the eight !SYM locations is a function of the location counter --
! each is the value written in its own SYN statement.  CHECKED, NOT
! ASSUMED: the deck was assembled three ways -- with the SLC as
! written, with it changed to "SLC,(8)7.0", and with the SLC line
! deleted outright -- and the symbol table came out BIT-IDENTICAL
! all three times.  I did NOT inherit
! p.101's sentence that "the counter is still 215000.00", because it
! is not true here: printed p.103 spent storage out to 215021.00.
! What the counter actually holds when p.108 is read is a question
! for the pages between, and this page cannot answer it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TAIL SCOPE: DMCP IS DEFINED TWICE IN THIS ASSEMBLY, AND BOTH ARE
! RIGHT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 5 defines D MCP as 32.0, i.e. 000040.00.  printed p.35 line 44
! defines D MCP as X24A at 001472.00, and printed pp.70, 75, 79 and
! 97 all branch to it there ("B,DMCP" assembling 001472.10 00).
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." put pp.99+ OUTSIDE the
! TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37
! closed with UNTAIL,(2).  So this is a name legitimately redefined
! in a different tail scope, NOT a collision and NOT an error in
! either transcription.  RECORDED, NOT FIXED.  A merge that puts this
! deck and p.35's in one symbol table without honouring tail scope
! will see a duplicate; that is the merge's problem to solve, not
! this page's.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS: WHAT WAS SETTLED AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) THE LOCATION AND BINARY COLUMNS ARE OCTAL, so every round glyph
!     in them is a 0 with certainty.  At 600 dpi this page prints
!     "OCCC4C.CO+" for 000040.00+ and "+OCCCOOCO" for +00000000 --
!     it drops ink on round glyphs constantly.  That calibrates the
!     page, it does NOT license converting any particular C elsewhere
!     (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "BE PRECISE ABOUT WHAT THE
!     GAUGE IS").
!
! (2) C vs D IN THE NAME COLUMN, SETTLED BY THE LEFT SIDE AT 1200
!     DPI, NOT BY INK LEVEL.  Six glyphs were cropped out of the name
!     column at 1200 dpi and montaged side by side at 500%:
!
!       line  5, the C of "MCP"      -- ROUND left side, curved
!                                       corners, no stem      -> C
!       line  9, the 3rd of "STDMOD" -- STRAIGHT vertical left
!                                       stem, square corners  -> D
!       line  9, the D of "MOD"      -- same shape             -> D
!       line 10, the 3rd of "S DD"   -- same shape             -> D
!       line 10, the 4th of "S DD"   -- same shape             -> D
!       line  8, the D of "DEN"      -- same shape             -> D
!
!     At 400 dpi lines 9 and 10 read "STCMOD" and "S CD"; both are
!     the worn-bowl D of printed p.93, and the C of MCP on line 5 is
!     visibly a different letter in the same column on the same page.
!
! (3) THE COMMENT COLUMN AGREES WITH ALL OF IT, independently:
!       line  6  "S INST D"  -INSTALLATION DENSITY - HIGH
!       line  7  "S INSTM"   -INSTALLATION MODE-NECC EVEN
!       line  8  "S TD DEN"  -STANDARD DENSITY * 1-LOW, 0-HIGH
!       line  9  "STDMOD"    -STANDARD MODE  NECC,ODD
!       line 10  "S DD"      -DISK DENSITY * 0-LOW, 1-HIGH
!       line 11  "SYSTAP"    -SYSTEM TAPE
!       line 12  "S FP"      -FILE PROTECT
!     DENSITY/MODE/DISK/STANDARD are all English words with a D in
!     them, and the names abbreviate the comments letter for letter.
!     Line 5 has NO comment, which is why its two round glyphs had to
!     be settled on shape alone -- and the spelling DMCP is
!     corroborated OFF THIS PAGE by five decks (pp.35, 70, 75, 79,
!     97), which is the preferred evidence per the brief.
!
! (4) "NECC" in lines 7 and 9's comments is transcribed as printed.
!     I did not decide what it abbreviates.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ARITHMETIC, CHECKED BOTH WAYS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A SYN value written bare is DECIMAL and the LOCATION column prints
! it OCTAL (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A BIT OFFSET IS OCTAL
! INSIDE (8), DECIMAL ONLY WHEN BARE").  Every row closes:
!
!   line  5  SYN,32.0        word 32 dec = 40 oct  -> 000040.00+
!   line  6  SYN(BU,24),0.0  word  0               -> 000000.00+
!   line  7  SYN(BU,24),2.0  word  2               -> 000002.00+
!   line  8  SYN(BU,1),0     word  0               -> 000000.00+
!   line  9  SYN(BU,24),3.0  word  3               -> 000003.00+
!   line 10  SYN(BU,7),0     word  0               -> 000000.00+
!   line 11  SYN(BU,1),.27   bit 27 dec = 33 oct   -> 000000.33+
!   line 12  SYN(BU,1),.26   bit 26 dec = 32 oct   -> 000000.32+
!
! and the data descriptions close the same way, 0o30 = 24 and
! 0o07 = 7, so "BU,30 ,10" is SYN(BU,24) and "BU,07 ,10" is
! SYN(BU,7).  Line 5's SYN carries no mode, so its data description
! prints "NULL", exactly as printed p.103 line 51's "SYN,$" does.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS NOT CHECKED HERE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! listing_oracle has no renderer for a data description, so the
! "BU,30 ,10" / "BU,01 ,10" / "BU,07 ,10" / "NULL" column is NOT
! checked by anything below -- a SYN(BU,24) mistranscribed as
! SYN(BU,30) would pass silently, since the mode does not change the
! resolved location.  The lengths were read off the column and are
! recorded in the listing block; they are not independently verified.
! This is the same gap printed p.103's deck records.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NONE.  Every printed spelling on this page was accepted by
! strap_asm as printed, including the two forms this page introduces
! that pp.99-103 did not use:
!   * a MODELESS SYN WITH A VALUE, "SYN, 32.0" (p.103's modeless SYN
!     was "SYN,$"), and
!   * a BIT-ONLY SYN VALUE WITH NO WORD PART, "SYN(BU,1), .27".
! Both were assembled in isolation before this deck was written and
! both resolve to the printed location.  There is no substitution
! anywhere in this deck.

        SLC, (8)215000.0            ! NOT PRINTED ON THIS PAGE, and
                                     ! not a claim about where the
                                     ! counter stands.  Inert: no row
                                     ! below consumes storage and no
                                     ! !SYM depends on it.

! ---- *** MISCELLANEOUS SYSTEM SYMBOLS *** (lines 1-4) -------------
DMCP    SYN, 32.0                   ! line  5 (no comment printed)
SINSTD  SYN(BU,24), 0.0             ! line  6 -INSTALLATION DENSITY
                                     !           - HIGH
SINSTM  SYN(BU,24), 2.0             ! line  7 -INSTALLATION MODE-NECC
                                     !           EVEN
STDDEN  SYN(BU,1), 0                ! line  8 -STANDARD DENSITY *
                                     !           1-LOW, 0-HIGH
STDMOD  SYN(BU,24), 3.0             ! line  9 -STANDARD MODE
                                     !           NECC,ODD
SDD     SYN(BU,7), 0                ! line 10 -DISK DENSITY *
                                     !           0-LOW, 1-HIGH
SYSTAP  SYN(BU,1), .27              ! line 11 -SYSTEM TAPE
SFP     SYN(BU,1), .26              ! line 12 -FILE PROTECT

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- all eight definition lines, with the
! LOCATION, the BINARY OUTPUT and the data description exactly as
! printed.  Every line number prints with a trailing asterisk
! ("5*" .. "12*"), the line-number column, not a location mark.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  5  000040.00+  +00000000  NULL       D MCP    SYN,32.0
!   line  6  000000.00+  +00000000  BU,30 ,10  S INST D SYN(BU,24),0.0
!   line  7  000002.00+  +00000000  BU,30 ,10  S INSTM  SYN(BU,24),2.0
!   line  8  000000.00+  +00000000  BU,01 ,10  S TD DEN SYN(BU,1),0
!   line  9  000003.00+  +00000000  BU,30 ,10  STDMOD   SYN(BU,24),3.0
!   line 10  000000.00+  +00000000  BU,07 ,10  S DD     SYN(BU,7),0
!   line 11  000000.33+  +00000000  BU,01 ,10  SYSTAP   SYN(BU,1),.27
!   line 12  000000.32+  +00000000  BU,01 ,10  S FP     SYN(BU,1),.26
!
! THE FOUR COMMENT CARDS, for the record.  LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT
! are both empty on all four and the card prints raw from the NAME
! column on, so no field lines up.  Measured at 600 dpi by counting
! ink runs at the printer's 10-per-inch pitch:
!   line  1  "- " + 70 asterisks            (dash in the NAME column)
!   line  2  9 blanks + "- *** MISCELLANEOUS SYSTEM SYMBOLS ***"
!   line  3  "- " + 70 asterisks            (identical to line 1)
!   line  4  "-"   and nothing else
! Lines 1, 3 and 4 put the dash in the NAME column; LINE 2 PUTS IT 9
! CHARACTERS FURTHER RIGHT, which is one more instance of the finding
! printed pp.101 and 103 both record: THE DASH IS CARD TEXT, NOT A
! FLAG COLUMN.  The tells that do hold are that LOCATION and BINARY
! OUTPUT are both empty and the NAME column is empty on all four.

! ---- CHECKS, read by tests/verify_mcp_page.py 108 ------------------
! Eight symbols and no rows: a SYN deposits no storage word, so there
! is nothing for a !CHECK to look at.  Manufacturing one from the
! "+00000000" the BINARY OUTPUT column prints would be checking the
! printer, not the assembler.
!SYM   DMCP     000040.00
!SYM   SINSTD   000000.00
!SYM   SINSTM   000002.00
!SYM   STDDEN   000000.00
!SYM   STDMOD   000003.00
!SYM   SDD      000000.00
!SYM   SYSTAP   000000.33
!SYM   SFP      000000.32
